From c776d763e5962f30324218d760f7b230ecab6d33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yusheng Peng <jiusi0519@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:03:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rclpy: do not link -latomic with the OHOS NDK clang (musl
 has no separate libatomic)

The NDK musl sysroot has no standalone libatomic (atomic builtins are in
libc), so the Clang branch now also requires NOT OHOS_CROSS_BUILD.

Reuse notes (cross-building rclpy / rosidl_generator_py extensions):
- The workspace build (scripts/build_ohos.sh) points Python3_INCLUDE_DIR /
  Python3_LIBRARY / Python3_SOABI at the board's CPython 3.12 sysroot copy
  (python_target/usr, pulled by scripts/pull_python_target.sh from the
  Jiusi-pys/python RK3588A port) while keeping Python3_EXECUTABLE = the
  host pixi python for code generation.
- PYTHON_MODULE_EXTENSION=.cpython-312-aarch64-linux-ohos.so must be set
  because pybind11 queries the HOST interpreter for EXT_SUFFIX (which
  would produce a win_amd64 .pyd name on a Windows host).
- On the board, extension modules only import because env.sh LD_PRELOADs
  libpython3.12.so.1.0: the Jiusi-pys launcher dlopen()s libpython with
  RTLD_LOCAL, so Py* symbols would otherwise not be globally visible.
---
 rclpy/CMakeLists.txt | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/rclpy/CMakeLists.txt b/rclpy/CMakeLists.txt
index 06c08deb09574e23f4bc75512d8b4fbcf3c7f89d..f53023bb38290726691593e29437397f404c0b71 100644
--- a/rclpy/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/rclpy/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -112,7 +112,9 @@ pybind11_add_module(_rclpy_pybind11
   src/rclpy/wait_set.cpp
 )
 
-if(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang" AND NOT APPLE)
+# OHOS cross build: the NDK musl sysroot has no standalone libatomic;
+# atomic builtins are provided by libc, so skip the extra link.
+if(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "Clang" AND NOT APPLE AND NOT OHOS_CROSS_BUILD)
   target_link_libraries(_rclpy_pybind11 PRIVATE atomic)
 endif()
 
-- 
