--- /dev/null
+++ b/rclpy/docs/type_description_service_lifetime.md
@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@
+# Type-description service ownership
+
+The native type-description service previously used a default-deleting
+`shared_ptr<rcl_service_t>`. Releasing its last `Service` wrapper freed that
+small handle without calling `rcl_service_fini()`, leaving the request reader
+and response writer alive after their node disappeared.
+
+The shared object now owns a finalizer that retains a native `Node` copy,
+calls `rcl_service_fini()`, then deletes the service handle. `get_impl()` copies
+share this lifetime; destroying one wrapper cannot finalize a service still
+owned by another. Zero initialization precedes shared-pointer construction,
+so initialization or later allocation failure also uses the same cleanup path.
+
+`test/test_type_description_service_lifetime.py` runs two independent unittest
+cases, each with alpha and observer in one live Context. Both keep the default
+type-description service enabled. The tests check global service discovery,
+the native request-reader/response-writer pair, and observer/Context validity
+after node destruction and after release of the last retained `get_impl()` copy.
+The assertions do not use `Context.destroy()` or garbage collection.
+
+## Local RK3588A evidence, 2026-09-06
+
+The ROS workspace contains the complete artifacts under
+`ohos_test_logs/type_description_lifetime/<run>/`. Each run records the actual
+Python child's exit, loaded library paths/hashes, fixture hash and graph phases.
+
+| Run | Result | `lifetime.log` SHA-256 |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `td_lifetime_red_20260906_01` | Both cases fail: service and both endpoints remain after final release; actual exit 1 | `742594cc1f679a21944839824fb684c6149c643b80512388a8553f4d1288c7fd` |
+| `td_lifetime_green_20260906_01` | Both cases pass, all five graph phases match; actual exit 0 | `83bca57ca7568e8c81bc0295fdc3255e98a298a9d7c1f16266b3ad54b4533465` |
+
+Both `host_verification.json` files report valid evidence with no evidence
+errors; GREEN also reports no functional errors. The unchanged test SHA-256 is
+`73060118067f7e0f28adde885c9befedd99886585c90c7b44fa207ce7bab8b92`.
+The packaged Python files, MDDS/RMW libraries, profile and test are identical
+between RED and GREEN. Only the rclpy native extension in `rclpy_overlay.tar`
+differs; its bytes were checked against `rclpy_package.json` and the process's
+recorded before/after mappings:
+
+- RED: `_rclpy_pybind11.cpython-312-aarch64-linux-ohos.so` SHA-256
+  `474a481d1934c7d719a433051afcc2f1abcc0f633afe717e2d046da346b722bd`,
+  matching the existing `install_ohos/Lib/site-packages/rclpy` extension.
+- GREEN: the extension SHA-256 is
+  `e95eb339d4f8e0da438be2bbdfeb8fb34fd96163efbf3467d3e44b6039efcdc7`,
+  matching `build_ohos/rclpy/test_rclpy` and loaded from the run's private
+  `/data/local/tmp/ros2/.mdds-owned-runs/td_lifetime_green_20260906_01/python/rclpy/`.
+
+This verifies same-Context ownership on KaihongOS using `rmw_mdds`, domain 51
+and the `ohos_dsoftbus` profile. Allocation-failure cleanup is covered by ownership
+design, not by fault-injection evidence in these two tests.
+
+The separate complete local broker integration also passed in
+`ohos_test_logs/broker_local/bl_fixed_rclpy_20260906_01/`. Two contexts exchanged
+five samples in each direction and completed ACK waits; alpha retirement removed
+its graph state, and beta then communicated with a fresh gamma context. The two
+independent worker processes passed their exact-payload and explicit completion
+barriers, including beta observing alpha's retirement. All three ROS children
+and the daemon exited 0, with daemon cleanup passing. Before/after process maps
+verified the same repaired native extension in the run's private rclpy package.
+The `contexts.log` SHA-256 is
+`99e8443e79275f4f8e893c6c9837c53b4181f1e3067715671b2ba3e3afd05c1d`;
+the sibling `alpha.log`, `beta.log`, status JSON and `evidence.sha256` retain the
+independent-process evidence.
+
+The broker run explicitly records `physical_dsoftbus_proven=false`; these local
+gates do not establish cross-board data delivery. Neither private-overlay run
+replaced the shared installed native extension.
diff --git a/rclpy/src/rclpy/type_description_service.cpp b/rclpy/src/rclpy/type_description_service.cpp
index 8dc354f130989d97ecf665e03a9f7fcf6a2a132d..95e03470384adc38d56ac264376017c2bf0ce4a5 100644
--- a/rclpy/src/rclpy/type_description_service.cpp
+++ b/rclpy/src/rclpy/type_description_service.cpp
@@ -14,6 +14,11 @@
 
 #include <pybind11/pybind11.h>
 
+#include <rcl/error_handling.h>
+#include <rcl/service.h>
+
+#include <memory>
+
 #include "type_description_service.hpp"
 #include "utils.hpp"
 
@@ -22,7 +27,22 @@ namespace rclpy
 
 TypeDescriptionService::TypeDescriptionService(Node & node)
 {
-  auto srv_ptr = std::make_shared<rcl_service_t>();
+  // Every get_impl() value shares this service and its finalizer. Keep the
+  // native node alive until rcl_service_fini has removed both RMW endpoints,
+  // including when the Python Node has already requested destruction.
+  auto srv_ptr = std::shared_ptr<rcl_service_t>(
+    new rcl_service_t(rcl_get_zero_initialized_service()),
+    [node](rcl_service_t * service)
+    {
+      const rcl_ret_t ret = rcl_service_fini(service, node.rcl_ptr());
+      if (RCL_RET_OK != ret) {
+        PyErr_WarnFormat(
+          PyExc_RuntimeWarning, 1, "Failed to fini type description service: %s",
+          rcl_get_error_string().str);
+        rcl_reset_error();
+      }
+      delete service;
+    });
   rcl_ret_t ret = rcl_node_type_description_service_init(srv_ptr.get(), node.rcl_ptr());
   if (RCL_RET_OK != ret) {
     throw RCLError("Failed to initialize type description service");
diff --git a/rclpy/test/test_type_description_service_lifetime.py b/rclpy/test/test_type_description_service_lifetime.py
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..7c758c58ee8afef2cbfa5cfd067117163fb3b521
--- /dev/null
+++ b/rclpy/test/test_type_description_service_lifetime.py
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+# Copyright 2026 Yusheng Peng
+#
+# Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the "License");
